From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tcdent <tcdent@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:47:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/38] rust: fs: abstractions for implementing file systems

Lets a file system be written in Rust: registration of a file system
type, superblock setup with per-superblock data, inodes with per-inode
data allocated from a dedicated slab cache, dentries, lookup and
revalidate, directory iteration, seek, get_link, statfs, and read_folio
into page-cache folios. Includes the folio wrapper and a kmem_cache
wrapper (mem_cache) the inode code needs.

Ported from Wedson Almeida Filho's "Rust abstractions for VFS" RFC v2
(May 2024, 30 patches) onto the 7.2 kernel crate. Differences from the
RFC: File is not parameterised by file system (callbacks take the
untyped File plus a typed INode); block-device superblocks, the inode
Mapper, xattrs and i_link storage are left out; get_link returns an
owned CString; inode attributes live in inode::Attr and can be refreshed
on a live inode; dentry::Operations with revalidate is new; const
operation tables use ..zeroed() instead of spelling every field.

This is one commit for now and will be split along the RFC's seams
before posting.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SKmspe5nVbuvzdvYZa9UhW
